 Bojenlinie der Ruderstrecke, folgt dem Fluss nach Süden unter der Versorgungsbrücke, den Bahnbrücken der Tōkaidō-Linie und dem Seta-gawa-Ōhashi hindurch zum Seta-no-Karahashi, einer der berühmtesten alten Brücken Japans, und weiter unter Shinkansen und Meishin-Autobahn bis zur Wende. Hinter dem Westufer steigen bewaldete Hügel an. Auf dem Wasser fahren Ausflugsschiffe und Motorboote.", "en": "At the southern tip of Lake Biwa, Japan's largest lake, the Seta River begins: Ōtsu's rowing water, lined with university and club boathouses. The course starts on the lake at the buoy line of the rowing course, follows the river south under the utility bridge, the Tōkaidō Line railway bridges and the Seta-gawa Ōhashi to the Seta-no-Karahashi, one of Japan's most famous old bridges, and on under the Shinkansen and the Meishin Expressway to the turn. Wooded hills rise behind the west bank. Tour boats and motorboats share the water."}, "highlights": [{"name": {"de": "Biwa-See", "en": "Lake Biwa"}, "side": "voraus", "note": {"de": "am Start, auf der Rückfahrt voraus", "en": "at the start, ahead on the way back"}}, {"name": {"de": "Seta-no-Karahashi mit der Insel Nakanoshima", "en": "Seta-no-Karahashi and Nakanoshima island"}, "side": "rechts"}, {"name": {"de": "Bootshäuser am Fluss", "en": "Boathouses along the river"}, "side": "beide"}, {"name": {"de": "Bewaldete Hügel am Westufer", "en": "Wooded hills on the west bank"}, "side": "rechts", "note": {"de": "vor der Wende", "en": "before the turn"}}], "bridges": ["Seta-gawa Kyōdō-bashi", "JR-Tōkaidō-Linie (zwei Brücken)", "Seta-gawa-Ōhashi", "Seta-no-Karahashi", "Tōkaidō-Shinkansen", "Meishin-Autobahn"]}